---
const steps = [
  "Run install.ps1 on each laptop, then restart Premiere.",
  "Open the panel: Window > Extensions > Tandem.",
  "Connect the laptops with Tailscale.",
  "Host: start the relay, then click Host in the panel.",
  "Guest: enter the host's address and your name, then click Connect.",
];
---

<section id="try" aria-labelledby="try-title">
  <h2 id="try-title" class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Try it</h2>
  <p class="mb-4">
    You need two Windows laptops with Premiere Pro, and Node.js on the host.
  </p>
  <ol class="steps steps-vertical">
    {steps.map((s) => <li class="step step-primary">{s}</li>)}
  </ol>
  <p class="mt-6">
    Edit something. Your partner's Premiere changes within about a second.
  </p>
  <a
    class="btn btn-outline btn-sm mt-6"
    href="https://github.com/jakecashion/hacklanta"
    target="_blank"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
  >
    Get the code on GitHub
    <span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span>
    <svg
      aria-hidden="true"
      class="h-3.5 w-3.5"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
    >
      <path d="M15 3h6v6M10 14L21 3M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6" />
    </svg>
  </a>
</section>
